{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Go to meet Moses, etc.</b> And although HaShem had said to him beforehand (Exodus 4:14) ״הִנֵּה הוּא יוֹצֵא״ etc., according to what is known to us — that HaShem speaks many things in a single utterance — at the time He said to Moses ״הִנֵּה הוּא״ etc., another utterance went forth to Aaron in Egypt. And there is no doubt that this prophecy was spoken to Aaron, although they of blessed memory said (Torat Kohanim 1) that wherever it says ״וַיְדַבֵּר ה׳ אֶל מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל אַהֲרֹן״ the utterance was spoken only to Moses, that he should tell Aaron, and even according to Rabbi Yosei HaGelili who holds (ibid.) that Aaron was excluded even from the utterances spoken in Egypt — that is specifically regarding matters pertaining to the mission to others; but this particular matter, that Aaron should perform a commandment — behold, it stands before you that HaShem spoke to him directly, and from this you learn that he was a prophet in his own right."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:37.366820332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}